kosha room

  -- an enclosed space bounded by walls, floor, and ceiling.
  -- the fundamental unit of built indoor space.
  -- a room defines a closed system for indoor physics:
  --   fixed volume (approximately): air pressure equilibrates with outside via gaps
  --   gravity acts inside exactly as outside
  --   temperature is relatively uniform (well-mixed air)
  --   all falling objects eventually reach the floor
  --
  -- a room is a container for air, for people, for objects.
  -- acoustics: sound reflects from walls, floor, ceiling — reverberation.
  -- thermally: room temperature = the baseline of all everyday thermal questions.
  --   "room temperature" = 20°C (293K) — the default condition in the kosha.

  "structures-varga-vishesa"
